    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Adenocarcinoma of the prostate, NCCN unfavorable intermediate risk: cT1c, Grade Group 3 (Gleason 4+3), PSA 6.4 ng/mL, 3 of 14 cores, found after a rising PSA; synthetic modern detail linked to his publicly announced prostate cancer</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C61</td><td>S — Synthetic grade, PSA, core count, stage, and risk group; the PSA rise, the biopsy-proven localized cancer that was not high grade, hormone therapy, and curative radiotherapy are from his doctors&apos; and spokeswoman&apos;s public statements (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Hormone-sensitive prostate cancer</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z19.1</td><td>S — Synthetic status in the modern episode.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Short-term androgen deprivation therapy (six months, leuprolide), with monitoring of testosterone, bone density, metabolic and cardiovascular risk, hot flashes, mood, and cognition</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z79.899</td><td>S — Synthetic androgen deprivation plan; Z79.899 is used because ICD-10-CM has no specific code for GnRH agonist therapy.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>History of pulmonary tuberculosis, treated, with no symptoms since</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z86.11</td><td>S — The 1988 tuberculosis is documented (D); the coding and the statement that it has not recurred are synthetic.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

